0\u0000\u0000�N\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000�%\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000�%\u0000\u0000\f\u0000\u0000\u0000�n\u0003�K\n�\u00016\b\u0000\u0000`\u001c\u0000\u0000�$\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000�&\u0000\u0000R\u0000\u0000\u0000�M\u0000\u0000>\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000�N\u0000\u0000L\u0001\u0000\u0000�Y\u0000\u00000\u0000\u0000\u0000�Y\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000�M\u0000\u0000\u0016\u0001\u0000\u0000\u0017^\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000='\u0000\u0000�\u0002\u0000\u0000\u0017^\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000�N\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000�)\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u00004\u0007\u0000\u0000�\u0000\u0000\u0000�\u0007\u0000\u0000r\u0000\u0000\u0000�\u0006\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000�\u0006\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000�\u0006\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000�\u0006\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0002\u0000�\u0000\u0000\u0000M I N U T E S\r\rIRVINE\rCITY COUNCIL REGULAR MEETING\r\rJanuary 25, 2005\r\r\f\rCALL TO ORDER \r\rA regular meeting of the Irvine City Council was called to order on January 25, 2005, at 4:03 p.m., in the City Council Chamber, Irvine Civic Center, One Civic Center Plaza, Irvine, California, Mayor Krom, presiding officer.\r\r\rROLL CALL\r \rPRESENT:\u00075\u0007COUNCILMEMBER:\u0007Larry Agran\u0007\u0007\u0007\u0007COUNCILMEMBER:\u0007Steven Choi\u0007\u0007\u0007\u0007COUNCILMEMBER:\u0007Christina Shea\u0007\u0007\u0007\u0007MAYOR PRO TEM:\u0007Sukhee Kang \u0007\u0007\u0007\u0007MAYOR:\u0007Beth Krom\r\u0007\u0007ABSENT:\u00070\u0007COUNCILMEMBER\u0007None\u0007\u0007\rAlso present were City Manager, Allison Hart; Assistant City Manager, Sean Joyce; Assistant City Manager, Wally Kreutzen; City Attorney, Joel Kuperberg; Director of Public Safety, David L. Maggard, Director of Administrative Services, Rick Paikoff; Director of Public Works, Marty Bryant; Acting Director of Community Services, John McAllister; Director of Community Development, Tina Christiansen; City Clerk, Jeri L. Stately; Deputy City Clerk, Teri Beach; and Sergeant At Arms, Christine D�alena. \r\rRECESS TO AN ADJOURNED SPECIAL MEETING OF THE IRVINE REDEVELOPMENT AGENCY � \r\rMayor Krom recessed the meeting to an adjourned special meeting of the Irvine Redevelopment Agency at 4:06 p.m.\r\rPlease refer to the Irvine Redevelopment Agency Minutes.\r\r\r\rRECONVENE CITY COUNCIL MEETING\r\rMayor Krom reconvened the meeting to the regular session of the Irvine City Council at 4:20 p.m.\r\r\rADDITIONS AND DELETIONS\r\rThere were no additions or deletions to the agenda.\r\r\rPUBLIC COMMENTS ON CONSENT CALENDAR ITEMS \r\rThere was no public comment on Consent Calendar items.\r\r\rAPPROVAL OF CONSENT CALENDAR ITEMS \r\rHearing no objections from other Councilmember�s, Mayor Krom removed the following items from the Consent Calendar for separate discussion and action:\r\r3.2 A DRAINAGE MAINTENANCE AGREEMENT WITH THE IRVINE COMPANY AND QUAIL HILL COMMUNITY ASSOCIATION COVERING A PORTION OF LOT A, TRACT MAP NO. 16225 AND PRESERVATION AREA H (QUAIL HILL, PLANNING AREA 17) (See Page 3 for action on this item.)\r\r3.3 CONSULTANT SERVICES AGREEMENT WITH NESTANDE CONSULTING (See Page 4 for action on this item.)\r\rACTION: It was moved by Mayor Pro Tempore Kang, seconded by Councilmember Choi, and unanimously carried to approve Consent Calendar Item Nos. 1 through 6.2, with the exception of Items as noted above.\r\rCITY COUNCIL MINUTES\r\rAPPROVAL OF CITY COUNCIL MINUTES (Submitted by City Clerk)\r\rACTION:\rApproved the minutes of a special meeting of the Irvine City Council held on January 7, 2005.\r\rApproved the minutes of a regular meeting of the Irvine City Council held on January 11, 2005.\u000b\r\rPROCLAMATIONS/COMMENDATIONS/RATIFICATIONS\r\rCOMMENDED THE FOLLOWING:\r\rOfficial Dedication of the Saddleback College Health Sciences Building - February 11, 2005\r\rPROCLAIMED THE FOLLOWING:\r\rAmerican Heart Association's National \"Wear Red Day For Women\" - February 4, 2005\r\r\rAGREEMENTS\r\rFUND EXCHANGE AGREEMENT BETWEEN THE ORANGE COUNTY TRANSPORTATION AUTHORITY AND THE CITY OF IRVINE (Submitted by Public Works/Transportation Development)\r\rACTION:\rCONTRACT NO. 4953 - Approved the Fund Exchange Agreement between the Orange County Transportation Authority and the City of Irvine.\r\rApproved the budget adjustment to allocate $6.85 million of federal Regional Surface Transportation Program (RSTP) funding to CIP 321210 and $1.4 million of federal RSTP funding to CIP 322740. Established a new CIP account to set aside $6.85 million of Gas Tax, Measure M Turnback and Systems Development Charges from CIP 321210 and $1.4 million of Gas Tax and Developer Fees & Exactions from CIP 322740 to be used to reimburse the Orange County Transportation Authority.\r\r\rCouncilmember Shea left the dais at 4:22 p.m.\r\r\rA DRAINAGE MAINTENANCE AGREEMENT WITH THE IRVINE COMPANY AND QUAIL HILL COMMUNITY ASSOCIATION COVERING A PORTION OF LOT A, TRACT MAP NO. 16225, AND PRESERVATION AREA H (QUAIL HILL, PLANNING AREA 17) (Submitted by Public Works/Development Engineering)\r\rACTION: It was moved by Mayor Pro Tempore Kang, seconded by Councilmember Choi and carried by those members present to:\r\rCONTRACT NO. 4954 - Approve a Drainage Maintenance Agreement between the City of Irvine, The Irvine Company, and Quail Hill Community Association, and authorize the Mayor to execute and the City Clerk to attest said agreement, subject to the City Attorney approval as to form.\r\rCouncilmember Shea returned to the dais at 4:23 p.m.\r\rCONSULTANT SERVICES AGREEMENT WITH NESTANDE CONSULTING (Submitted by City Manager)\r\rThis item was removed from the Consent Calendar at the request of Councilmember Choi who noted he received correspondence that Mr. Nestande was a proponent of an airport at MCAS � El Toro and requested clarification of the City�s decision to award the contract, to which Daniel Jung, Director of Strategic Programs, responded. (Exhibit No. 1 on file in the City Clerk�s Department)\r\rDirected staff to schedule a meeting with the consultant and members of the City Council.\r\rACTION: It was moved by Councilmember Choi, seconded by Mayor Pro Tempore Kang, and unanimously carried to:\r\rCONTRACT NO. 4959 - Authorize the Mayor to sign and the City Clerk to attest to a professional services consultant agreement with Nestande Consulting, subject to the City Attorney approval as to form.\r\rALLOCATION OF FUNDS\r\rURBAN AREA SECURITY INITIATIVE 2004 GRANT (Submitted by Public Safety/Administration)\r\rACTION:\rAccepted an Urban Area Security Initiative 2004 grant award in the amount of $22,817.\r\rApproved a budget adjustment request in the amount of $22,817, reflecting $22,817 in revenues and appropriations.\r\rREPORTS\r\rDUES FOR THE ORANGE COUNTY COUNCIL OF GOVERNMENTS (Submitted by CMO/Strategic Programs)\r\rACTION: Directed the City Manager to pay the City's 2004 dues to the Orange County Council of Governments\r\rRESOLUTIONS\r\rWARRANT AND WIRE TRANSFER RESOLUTION (Submitted by Administrative Services/Fiscal Services)\r\rACTION: Adopted a Resolution entitled: RESOLUTION NO. 05-08 - A RESOLUTION OF THE CITY COUNCIL OF THE CITY OF IRVINE ALLOWING CERTAIN CLAIMS AND DEMANDS AND SPECIFYING THE FUNDS OUT OF WHICH THE SAME ARE TO BE PAID.\r\rA RESOLUTION OF THE CITY COUNCIL OF THE CITY OF IRVINE ESTABLISHING THE ORDER OF BUSINESS OF CITY COUNCIL MEETINGS (Submitted by CMO/City Clerk)\r\rACTION: Approved the proposed policy amendment and adopted resolution entitled: RESOLUTION NO. 05-09 - A RESOLUTION OF THE CITY COUNCIL OF THE CITY OF IRVINE ESTABLISHING THE ORDER OF BUSINESS OF CITY COUNCIL MEETINGS\r\r\rEND OF CONSENT CALENDAR\r\r\rCOUNCIL BUSINESS\r\rREPORTS - BUSINESS\r\rNON-ECONOMIC SPONSORSHIP OF THE AMERICAN CANCER SOCIETY RELAY FOR LIFE - MAY 21-22, 2005 (This item was agendized for discussion by Mayor Krom)\r\rJoanne Slobodien and Christine Carbonel Schaubach representing American Cancer Society, gave a brief presentation on the American Cancer Society Relay for Life. \r\rACTION: It was moved by Mayor Krom, seconded by Councilmember Choi, and unanimously carried to:\r\rApprove the non-economic sponsorship for the upcoming American Cancer Society fundraiser, �Relay for Life.�\r\r\r\r\r\rACTIONS RELATED TO ADOPTION OF THE REDEVELOPMENT PLAN FOR THE ORANGE COUNTY GREAT PARK REDEVELOPMENT PROJECT AREA\r\rCity Council discussion included clarification of waiver of first reading of ordinance. \r\rACTION: It was moved by Councilmember Agran, seconded by Councilmember Choi, and unanimously carried to:\r\rAdopt a resolution entitled:\r\r RESOLUTION NO. 05-10 - A RESOLUTION OF THE CITY COUNCIL OF THE CITY OF IRVINE ADOPTING WRITTEN RESPONSES TO WRITTEN OBJECTIONS ON THE REDEVELOPMENT PLAN FOR THE ORANGE COUNTY GREAT PARK REDEVELOPMENT PROJECT AREA\u000b\rWaive the reading of the ordinance and Introduce for first reading and read by title only an ordinance entitled:\r\rORDINANCE NO. 05-04 - AN ORDINANCE OF THE CITY COUNCIL OF THE CITY OF IRVINE APPROVING AND ADOPTING THE REDEVELOPMENT PLAN FOR THE ORANGE COUNTY GREAT PARK REDEVELOPMENT PROJECT AREA \r\r*PUBLIC HEARINGS\r\rPUBLIC HEARING: ZONING TEXT CHANGE FOR THE 6.1 INSTITUTIONAL DISTRICT (Submitted by: CMO/Director of Strategic Programs)\r\rMayor Krom opened the public hearing at 6:31 p.m.\r\rGlen Worthington, Principal Planner, presented the staff report.\r\rACTION: At 6:32 p.m., it was moved by Councilmember Shea, seconded by Councilmember Agran, and unanimously carried to close the public hearing.\r\rACTION: It was moved by Councilmember Shea, seconded by CouncilmemberAgran, and unanimously carried to:\r\rIntroduce for first reading and read by title only an ordinance entitled: ORDINANCE NO. 05-05 -AN ORDINANCE OF THE CITY COUNCIL OF THE CITY OF IRVINE APPROVING A ZONING TEXT CHANGE FOR THE 6.1 INSTITUTIONAL DISTRICT\r\rRECESS\r\rMayor Krom recessed the meeting to Closed Session at 4:48 p.m.\r\r\rCLOSED SESSION\r\rPUBLIC EMPLOYEE PERFORMANCE EVALUATION\r\rCITY MANAGER\r\r\rRECONVENE TO THE CITY COUNCIL MEETING \r\rMayor Krom reconvened the meeting to regular session at 5:46 p.m., and requested City Attorney announce action taken during the Closed Session.\r\rCity Attorney Joel Kuperberg announced:\r\rACTION: By unanimous vote, the City Council:\r\rFormally accepted a letter of resignation that City Manager Allison Hart presented to the Council last year with a retirement to be effective June 30, 2005;\rIn accordance with her contract, City Manager Allison Hart is granted a 10% merit increase retroactive to July, 2004, in accordance with paragraph 3.2 of that agreement based upon evaluation of performance and accomplishments since that date;\rCity Manager Allison Hart�s final day of work as City Manager will be June 30, 2005, to assist with the transition to a new City Manager and to complete on-going projects such as completion of MCAS � El Toro Base sale and working with the Department of the Navy. Allison Hart will continue as a City employee receiving full salary and benefits consistent with the terms of her employment agreement through December 30, 2005 and will be available on site as needed during this time.\r\r\r\rPLEDGE OF ALLEGIANCE\r\rMayor Pro Tempore Kang led the Pledge of Allegiance.\r\r\r\rMOMENT OF SILENCE\r\rMayor Krom requested a moment of silence.\r\r\rMUSICAL PRESENTATION\r\rMayor Krom introduced Irvine Idol Winner Alexandria Giusto who performed, \"The National Anthem.\"\r\r\rINTRODUCTIONS\r\rCouncilmember Choi introduced his commission/committee/staff appointees as follows:\rPlanning Commissioner, Adam Probolsky\rCommunity Services Commissioner, Jeannie Luong \rFinance Commissioner, David Sparks\rSenior Citizen�s Council, Alireza Jazayeri\rInvestment Committee Member, Douglas Kim\rChild Care Committee Member, Suzanna Choi\rCouncil Executive Assistant, Janet Colclaser \rCouncil Executive Assistant, Carl Berman\r\r\rANNOUNCEMENTS/COMMITTEE REPORTS/COUNCIL REPORTS\r\rMayor Pro Tempore Kang made the following announcements:\rRandy Kiefer, an Irvine resident, sent a letter recognizing Katie Berg, Rick Sandzimeier and Mike Loving of Public Works, for the professional and attentive manner in which his request on bicycle related issues was handled;\rOn Saturday, January 22, he and his Council Executive Assistant, Subia Aleem, participated in a Ride-Along with Police Officers Mario Casas and Johanna Soto. He noted that Commander Jeff Kermode met them at the Irvine spectrum and gave them a complete tour of the sub-station and the businesses. In addition, he commended the officers and the Irvine Police Department;\rThe Irvine Police Department will be conducting a 14-week course, �The Community Police Academy,� beginning March 30, 2005; interested individuals can contact the Public Safety Department for more information on enrolling in the program; and\rOn March 30, 2005, the City of Irvine will be hosting a forum, �City of Irvine Streets and Traffic: Where We Are, and Where We Are Going,� to be held in the City Council Chambers. The forum is designed to provide residents and the business community with information regarding the City�s current and future transportation plans. \r\r\r\r\r\rMayor Krom made the following announcements:\rThe City of Irvine is seeking nominations for Family Friendly Business Awards, the deadline for nominations is February 4, 2005;\rThe City of Irvine is accepting applications for its First Time Home Buyer Down-Payment Assistant Program through February 4, 2005; and\rThe Irvine Sister Cities Foundation is coordinating a student exchange home-stay program between Irvine and Tsukuba, Japan. A parent/student informational meeting will be held at City Hall in conference room L102, on Thursday, January 27 at 6:00 p.m. \r\r\rPUBLIC COMMENTS \r\rShowleh Tolbert, Irvine resident, expressed appreciation to the City for their support of the community project �The Irvine Community Cares,� organized to raise funds for the Tsunami victims in South Asia. \r\rVirginia Read, Irvine resident, spoke on employment issues.\r\rMitch Goldstone, Irvine resident, will be on Fox Network News on Wednesday, 9:30 AM (PT) for a live interview regarding his national campaign to raise 10,000 digital cameras for military families by Valentines day.\r\r\rRECESS\r\rMayor Krom recessed the meeting at 6:33 p.m.\r\r\rRECONVENE\r\rMayor Krom reconvened the meeting at 6:42 p.m. \r\r\rSTATE OF THE CITY ADDRESS\r\rMayor Krom presented the State of the City Address. (Exhibit No. 2 on file in the City Clerk�s Department.)\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\rADJOURNMENT\r\rAt 7:35 p.m., by consensus, the City Council adjourned to a CITY COUNCIL REGULAR meeting, February 8, 2005, 4:00 p.m., City of Irvine, City Council Chamber, One Civic Center Plaza, Irvine, California.\r\r\r\r ________________________________\r MAYOR OF THE CITY OF IRVINE\r\r\r\r\r____________________________________ _February 8, 2005__\rCITY CLERK OF THE CITY OF IRVINE DATE APPROVED\r\u0013 PAGE \u00142\u0015\r\rCity Council Minutes January 25, 2005\r\r\rPrepared by the City Clerk�s Office \u0013 PAGE \u00144\u0015\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0